'''ancient<sup>2</sup>†''' (ān′shent), ''n.'' [Early mod. E. also ''antient'', ''ancyent'', ''auncient'', ''auntient'', and even ''antesign'', corrupt forms of ''ensign'', in simulation of ''ancient''<sup>1</sup>: see ''ensign''.] '''1.''' A flag, banner, or standard; an ensign; especially, the flag or streamer of a ship.
{{smaller block|Ten times more dishonourable ragged than an old-faced [that is, patched] ''ancient''.
